% Drawn small, and quiet: this is for a scanner, and a student should
% not feel watched by it. `\cipcode` is what the footer calls.
\newcommand{\cipcode}{%
  \stepcounter{cipsheet}%
  % `nolink`, which is why it was cyan. `qrcode` sets
  % `\qr@hyperlinktrue` by default, wraps the code in a hyperref
  % link, and hyperref colours it -- so wrapping it in
  % `\textcolor{black}` changed nothing, because the colour was not
  % coming from the surrounding text. A payload of `CIP1*...` is not a
  % URL either, so the link was never meaningful.
  %
  % A scanner wants maximum contrast; light cyan on white is close to
  % the worst case a decoder can be handed.
  %
  % 9mm, not 7.5: 33 modules across 7.5mm is 0.23mm each, which a
  % 300dpi scan samples at under three pixels. Three is the floor
  % every decoder quotes, so it was sitting exactly on it.
  % 15mm, from a module measured off a 600dpi render rather than from
  % version arithmetic -- the package puts a quiet zone inside the
  % height it is given, so the data modules are smaller than
  % height/29 and the arithmetic was optimistic by a third.
  %
  % Measured at 12mm: 0.381mm per module, which is exactly 3.00
  % pixels at 200dpi. Three is the floor every decoder quotes, so
  % that was sitting on it with nothing in hand for a fold, a crease
  % or a photocopy. 15mm gives 0.476mm -- 3.75 pixels at 200dpi and
  % 5.6 at 300 -- which is room to be wrong in.
  %
  % Centred on the footer text rather than hung below it: `\raisebox`
  % by half the height, less half the x-height, puts the middle of the
  % square on the middle of the line.
  % Order matters. `\raisebox{-0.5\height}` measures the box it is
  % given, so the inner one has to be the raw symbol -- that puts its
  % middle on the baseline. Lifting by half an x-height then puts it
  % on the middle of the text. Nested the other way round, `\height`
  % was the already-shifted box and the code hung low.
  \raisebox{0.5ex}{\raisebox{-0.5\height}[0pt][0pt]{\textcolor{black}{%
    \qrcode[height=15mm, level=M, nolink]{\cippayload}}}}}

